Since most of the xd.shell.itests will do more then one thing (deploy a stream, start it, add a tap, add a job, stop, etc) we decided to decouple writing testcases with running it. Test cases will be written in spring-shell scriptlets. Scriptlets are json files with command and expectedResult as tokens.  Here's an example:

{code}
{ "testscript": 
 [ {"command" : "stream create --definition "http | file" --name http2file",
    "result" : "Created new stream 'http2file'"},
   {"command" : "stream list",
    "result" : "..."}
 ]
}
{code}

A parser will parse scriptlets, executes it and asserts on expected results.

